    intro: "When you scan a document with the wrong orientation or receive a PDF with sideways pages, the fix should be simple. But simply rotating the view in a PDF reader does not actually save the change. This guide explains how to permanently rotate pages so the file always opens correctly.",
    sections: [
      { heading: "Why PDF Pages Come Out Sideways", body: "The most common cause is scanning with the paper loaded in the wrong direction. Scanners capture the image as-is and embed it into the PDF at whatever angle it was fed. Some mobile scanning apps also default to landscape orientation.\n\nAnother common cause is receiving a PDF exported from software that used landscape page settings, or a camera-captured document where the phone was held sideways." },
      { heading: "Rotating the View vs. Rotating the File", body: "Most PDF readers let you rotate the view while reading. This is temporary — the rotation is not saved. If you email or print the file, it will revert to the original orientation.\n\nTo permanently fix the orientation, you need a tool that modifies the PDF structure and saves the rotation change into the file itself." },
      { heading: "How to Rotate a PDF Page Online", body: "Open the ToolMint Rotate PDF tool. Upload your PDF by clicking or dragging the file into the upload area. Select the pages you want to rotate — individual pages, a range, or all pages at once. Choose 90 degrees clockwise, 90 degrees counter-clockwise, or 180 degrees. Click Rotate and then Download.\n\nThe downloaded file has the permanent rotation applied. Every device and app will now open it in the correct orientation." },
      { heading: "Rotating Only Some Pages", body: "Most rotation tools let you select specific page ranges. If pages 3 and 7 of a 10-page document are sideways, you can rotate only those without affecting the rest.\n\nIf you need to rotate all pages in a large document, select all pages at once to save time. Rotating page by page is only necessary when different pages need different orientations." },
      { heading: "Rotating PDFs on a Phone", body: "The Rotate PDF tool works in any mobile browser. Open the page on your phone, upload the file from your camera roll or files app, choose the rotation angle, and download the fixed PDF. No app installation is required.\n\nFor scanning apps that produce sideways pages regularly, check your scanner app settings for an automatic orientation detection option." },
    ],
    faqs: [
      { q: "Does rotating a PDF change the file size?", a: "No. Rotation is a structural change to how the page is displayed. Image data is not re-encoded, so the file size stays the same." },
      { q: "Can I rotate only one page in a multi-page PDF?", a: "Yes. Choose the specific page number in the rotation tool. Only that page will be changed; all others stay as they are." },
      { q: "Why does my PDF look rotated in one app but not another?", a: "Some viewers save a display rotation preference locally and apply it automatically. The underlying file may still be in the wrong orientation. Use a rotation tool to fix the file itself." },
      { q: "Can I undo a rotation after saving?", a: "You can always re-rotate the downloaded file in the opposite direction. The original is unchanged unless you overwrite it." },
    ],
